# Pinned obsidian-headless CLI: exact version + SHA-256 of the artifacts.
#
# WHY A PIN AT ALL. Obsidian Sync rewrites the vault in place. An upstream
# data-loss report against obsidian-headless 0.0.12 is the reason this file
# exists: the agent will only ever run the ONE build whose contract was captured
# and whose bytes were attested, never "whatever `ob` happens to be on PATH".
#
# TWO CHECKSUMS, because two different things get verified at two different
# times:
#
#   tarball    the npm artifact `npm pack obsidian-headless@<version>` produces.
#              scripts/fetch-obsidian-headless.sh verifies THIS before it will
#              install anything, so a tampered registry mirror is caught at
#              staging time.
#   entrypoint the SHA-256 of the package's `cli.js`, which is the file node
#              actually executes. `vault.CLI.Verify` resolves the `ob` shim (an
#              npm symlink) to this file and checksums it on EVERY run, so a
#              binary swapped after installation is caught at run time. The
#              value is identical before and after `npm install` — the install
#              adds dependencies around cli.js, it does not rewrite it.
#
# The contract this exact build accepts is captured in
# internal/agent/vault/testdata/ob-<version>-contract.txt and asserted by
# TestArgvMatchesThePinnedContract, so the argv the agent emits cannot drift
# from the parser the pinned build ships.
#
# Bumping the pin:
#   1. scripts/fetch-obsidian-headless.sh --version <new> --record   (downloads,
#      prints both checksums; verify the tarball against upstream's own
#      published integrity value before recording it)
#   2. scripts/capture-ob-contract.sh <path-to-ob>                   (re-capture
#      the parser contract; review the diff — a removed flag is a breaking
#      change, not a formatting change)
#   3. Update this file and internal/agent/vault/cli_test.go's pin assertions.
#   4. Re-run the AUTHENTICATED disposable-vault smoke (task .7, needs Daniel's
#      Obsidian account) before pointing it at the real vault.
#
# Format: `key = value`, one per line, `#` comments ignored.
# `checksum = PENDING` is a hard refusal, not a warning (vault.ErrPinUnset).

version = 0.0.13
tarball = 9b8e1ad3917a65d53c5ab74d06acf5ec8d941e3b02bd9bd5d035d6800e533198
checksum = c7a0b843cd18f1164305a569d56164723a670b9ebcb66e6a445bb9fbf9555637
